WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.180
There had been quite a buzz at the SCP Foundation
when, only a few days ago, word had spread

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.460
of a possibly anomalous archaeological dig.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.580
Excavations at a redacted location in the
Middle East had unearthed what appeared to

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:19.600
be an ancient shrine, with a large stone tablet
as its centerpiece, inscribed with runes of

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.570
a language lost to the ages.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.939
Now, normally, this wouldn’t be nearly enough
to attract the interest of the Foundation,

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:30.689
especially without any overtly anomalous component
to the shrine.

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:36.040
Usually, this would pass unnoticed as just
a slightly interesting discovery that could

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.950
perhaps make its way to a museum.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:44.790
But along with the tablet were a pair of carvings
on the surface of the stone shrine.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:50.670
These depicted a pair of figures, seemingly
rivals that were locked together in an endless

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.680
cycle of conflict.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.430
And that was what caught the collective eye
of the Foundation: the figures in these carvings

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:06.290
seemed to bear a very close, almost uncanny
resemblance to SCP-073 and SCP-076, better

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:10.480
known respectively as Cain and Able.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.220
While the carvings were too large to be transported
in their entirety, the stone tablet bearing

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:19.120
its inscription was requisitioned by the SCP
Foundation.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.049
And almost immediately after it arrived, the
buzz surrounding it died down, focus shifting

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.720
to one of what was considered the far bolder
and more exciting anomalies.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.760
But one researcher – by the name of Isaac
Graves – remained solely focused on the

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.820
mysterious tablet.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.430
Researcher Graves was determined to be the
one who discovered the connection between

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:45.500
this stone and both SCP-073 and SCP-076.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:50.790
Many had long suspected that this pair of
anomalous immortals were related, brothers

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.000
even.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.940
Perhaps this tablet and the shrine it was
found in held the key to proving once and

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.790
for all if that long-standing theory was indeed
true.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:04.270
Of course, the biggest obstacle standing in
Graves’ way was: nobody knew how to read

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.860
what had been inscribed on the tablet.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:12.330
The language was runic, and so many thousands
of years old that there was no way of translating

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.489
it… or at least, no quick way.

00:02:15.489 --> 00:02:19.680
Understanding what was written on the stone
was going to take some time.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.519
Several years of tireless research passed,
with every day Researcher Graves spent studying

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:29.180
the tablet feeling like a step closer to revealing
its secrets.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:33.660
He had to become fluent in all the languages
spoken in the region where the shrine was

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.280
first discovered, along with all the variations
and dialects of each.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:43.190
Then, it was a case of working backwards,
finding the ancient roots of each of these

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.980
modern patterns of speech and writing.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:50.500
And eventually, after at last discovering
the right linguistic branch, going through

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.550
the inscription word by word to translate
it.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:59.100
It was only when he stepped back, and read
the tablet in its entirety, that Graves understood

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.310
what he was truly looking at.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:06.150
Realization dawning on him, the researcher
turned and barrelled through the facility

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.150
corridors.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:11.940
He demanded to speak urgently with the Site
Director, the Senior Research staff, and anyone

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.870
and everyone in authority who would listen.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:19.500
And all because what Researcher Graves had
found could render all prior study of two

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.480
prolific anomalies completely null and void.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:29.860
He believed that the tablet described the
true, tragic origin of both Cain and Able.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.670
As Graves gathered his various superiors,
he recounted what he had learned from the

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:34.860
tablet.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:39.939
Years and years ago, many millennia before
the dawn of modern civilization, there had

00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:41.989
lived an isolated family.

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:47.840
They lived in a small, rural homestead, maintained
a decent amount of farmland, and traded crops

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.549
and livestock with traders from a nearby township
in order to survive.

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:57.410
Two sons were eventually born to a mother
and father whose names were forgotten to the

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.420
annals of history.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:03.640
But their sons’ names, however, would not
only live on in legend, but would one day

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:07.110
refer to a pair of anomalous individuals.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:11.500
Of course, as most of the Foundation higher
up in the room quickly guessed, the two brothers

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.770
were named Cain and Able.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:18.620
Now, according to the legend Researcher Graves
had translated from the tablet, Cain was the

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.520
family’s firstborn son, and for a time,
the pride and joy of his mother and father.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.930
As he got older and reached an age where he
was able to, Cain began to help his father

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.550
tend the farmland around their home.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:35.570
Until, one day, Cain’s mother fell pregnant
again, with yet another son.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:40.210
However, the birth of this new child was fraught
with far more difficulty, and sadly claimed

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.220
the life of the boys’ mother.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.850
As his father held his newborn younger brother
in his arms, Cain stood by his mother’s

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.250
side as she passed away.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.320
His father named the new child Able, and raised
him as best as he could.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:58.199
However, the loss of his wife had stricken
him with grief, which took a toll on him as

00:04:58.199 --> 00:05:00.889
the years rolled on and Able grew up.

00:05:00.889 --> 00:05:06.330
It seemed with every passing day, as the young
boy grew into a man, time had the opposite

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.940
effect on his father.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:13.300
He became frail, unable to farm any longer,
causing Cain to take up maintaining the crops

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.400
in his father’s increasing absence.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.460
Until, one day, the father of the two boys
fell ill.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:24.370
Eventually succumbing to sickness, he too
died, reunited with his wife but leaving the

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:28.030
pair of brothers alone, with only each other.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:32.710
The final bit of wisdom their father had imparted
to Cain and Able was to trust in the old man

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:33.710
on the hill.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:38.590
Sure enough, a figure would often appear looking
down at the valley where they lived.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:44.569
According to their father, this man was the
Creator, the one who had made the world around

00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:48.540
them, all the heavens, and every part of the
universe’s majesty.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:54.169
He could control life and death, every force
of nature only existed and behaved in accordance

00:05:54.169 --> 00:05:56.219
with the Creator’s design.

00:05:56.219 --> 00:06:01.169
And before his eventual passing, Cain and
Able’s father had told his two sons that,

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:06.650
if they made a small sacrifice to the Creator,
then he would provide for them and watch over

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:07.889
the brothers.

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:12.349
And so, following their father’s wishes,
Cain and Able would regularly make their journey

00:06:12.349 --> 00:06:15.740
up the nearby hill, to where the old man resided.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.070
Sometimes he would speak with them, friendly
conversing while the two men made certain

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.120
to be as polite as they knew how to be.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:26.599
They would present the Creator with goats,
sheep, and all manner of livestock that they

00:06:26.599 --> 00:06:31.620
kept on their farm; their offering to him
in exchange for plentiful harvests and the

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.460
safe passage of their mother and father into
the great beyond.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:40.080
The Creator would tell either Cain or Able
to kill their offering, alternating between

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.509
each of the brothers every time.

00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:46.840
According to the stone tablet, back then,
this was in a time before man had learned

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:52.479
how to kill another man, not a single person
had ever murdered another… but that was

00:06:52.479 --> 00:06:54.400
soon to change.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.889
As the brothers grew up, Able reaching his
twenties and Cain just slightly older than

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:01.900
that, they continued to work on their homestead.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:06.789
Cain was still tending to his parent’s land,
farming crops to feed them both and sell at

00:07:06.789 --> 00:07:07.789
market.

00:07:07.789 --> 00:07:12.360
It was a hard, laborious life, the heat of
an unforgiving sun bearing down on him in

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.449
the fields.

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:18.870
Cain loathed it, every day was exhausting,
but he knew if he stopped, then he and his

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.210
brother would perish.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:23.900
Able, meanwhile, saw to the animals, becoming
a shepherd.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:29.389
In contrast to Cain’s attitude toward farming,
Able seemed to rather enjoy his work, herding

00:07:29.389 --> 00:07:30.389
the cattle.

00:07:30.389 --> 00:07:34.759
He had a good command over them, they listened
to what he said, and that seemed, at least

00:07:34.759 --> 00:07:38.889
to Cain, to make his younger brother’s job
unfairly easier.

00:07:38.889 --> 00:07:42.000
There was some disparity between Cain and
Able.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.120
The tablet didn’t state what had started
it; maybe it was simply the fact they stuck

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.780
so unmovably to their roles rather than alternating.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:54.540
Or perhaps it was a lingering resentment on
Cain’s part; after all, their mother had

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.430
died giving birth to Able, which could have
easily led to the older brother laying the

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.370
blame at his sibling’s feet.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:06.020
Even more so as losing his wife had been the
thing that started their father’s eventual

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:08.870
decline, causing him to die too.

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:13.509
But all was as the Creator willed it, Cain
told himself, although it did little to ease

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:18.520
the pain of his parents’ deaths… and did
little to stop what would happen next.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.650
Having grown jealous of his younger brother,
watching him enjoy his work herding the animals

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:27.310
and getting to rest for most of the day while
he slaved away, Cain decided to bring his

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.430
own sacrifice to the Creator.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:34.490
While Able readied a goat to be offered, much
like they had done numerous times before,

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:38.709
Cain gathered up the best of his crops from
the season, and the pair made their journey

00:08:38.709 --> 00:08:40.149
up the hill.

00:08:40.149 --> 00:08:44.360
Presenting the elderly man with both their
offerings, he seemed confused as to why there

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.700
was more this time.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:50.350
It may have been that the Creator interpreted
this as greed on the brothers’ part, bringing

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.820
him a greater offering in exchange for greater
reward.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.910
Or possibly just out of preference for the
type of sacrifice he accepted.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:02.480
But whatever the reason, the Creator seemed
to favor Able’s offering of the goat over

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.529
the crops Cain had presented.

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:09.779
The long walk back down into the valley was
tense, both brothers were silent.

00:09:09.779 --> 00:09:13.230
But it was clear to Able that something was
wrong with Cain.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:16.720
He was seething, practically shaking with
anger.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:20.720
Although the younger of the two could never
have predicted what his sibling would do next…

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.720
or that he’d never make it to the bottom
of the hill.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.770
In a blind fit of rage, Cain lunged at his
brother, attacking him out of spite at the

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.720
fact his sacrifice had been favored.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.500
In his hands, Able still held the blade used
to sacrifice his livestock to the Creator,

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.180
until Cain struck him.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.649
The knife clattered to the ground, only for
the elder of the brothers to reach for it.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:47.520
Completely overwrought with his anger, all
Cain could think was to do unto Able as they

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.420
had done to their other sacrifices, maybe
then the Creator would favor him instead of

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.050
his younger sibling.

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:59.180
The wise old man was initially horrified to
see Cain returning so soon, carrying the body

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:03.660
of Able over his shoulders which he then dumped
at the Creator’s feet.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:09.450
No one on Earth had ever killed a fellow human
being before, this was completely unprecedented.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.830
It was only when he saw the saddened look
in the old man’s eyes and his brother’s

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:18.839
corpse lying still on the ground that the
true gravity of what he had done hit Cain.

00:10:18.839 --> 00:10:23.320
He pleaded with the Creator to reverse what
he’d done, saying over and over again that

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:25.010
he had made a mistake.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:29.430
The old man agreed to oblige, perhaps knowing
or just believing that Cain hadn’t wanted

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.950
to kill Able.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:35.820
Controlling the forces of life and death itself,
he resurrected the younger of the brothers,

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:41.070
and in the process, turned him into a mighty
warrior, with an inexhaustible supply of weaponry

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:46.339
so that he would never be slain again and
could always defend himself from harm.

00:10:46.339 --> 00:10:50.970
However, the same rage that had possessed
Cain now took hold of Able.

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:55.709
With his newfound power, he immediately went
to exact a terrible, brutal vengeance on his

00:10:55.709 --> 00:10:56.920
brother.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.300
Witnessing the ferocity of the younger man,
and the horrible wounds Able inflicted on

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.140
Cain, the Creator was forced to intervene.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:08.490
As he had done before, he returned Cain to
life and repaired the damage to his body,

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:14.120
but saw it fit to punish both the brothers
for what they had done out of jealousy, anger,

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.350
and revenge.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:20.410
The old man deemed it so that neither one
of them could die; Able would fall but return

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:21.970
to life each time.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:26.410
Meanwhile, the Creator condemned Cain to wander
the Earth forever, but the man who had once

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:31.490
farmed and made the land fertile for crops
would never again get to witness the majesty

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:32.760
of nature.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:38.329
Wherever he went, the plants around Cain would
wither and die, while any wound that was inflicted

00:11:38.329 --> 00:11:43.430
upon him would be reflected back on the one
who caused it, as a constant reminder of the

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:48.750
harm he had done to his little brother, Able,
and thus started all this.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:53.140
After telling the legend in its entirety,
Researcher Graves led the Site Director and

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:57.580
Senior Researchers back to his lab where he
had been studying the stone tablet.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:02.610
They arrived just in time to see it crumbling
into dust, destroying all records of what

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:07.980
Graves had learned about SCP-073 and SCP-076.

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:12.930
The tragic story of how Cain and Able came
to be was lost forever.

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:15.370
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:18.720
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:25.570
Now go and check out “SCP-073 - Cain”
and “SCP-076 - Able” for more of these

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.040
ill-fated immortal brothers!

